## Infrastructure — Only Three Class Types Allowed

| Type | Responsibility | Allowed Logic |
|------|---------------|---------------|
| **Provider** | Data access / I/O (DB, API, cache, queue, file) | I/O only, no business logic |
| **Validator** | Validate I/O data before Provider or after external output | Validation only |
| **Transfer** | Transform data between layers / representations | Mapping only |

**No other class types are allowed in this layer.**

---

## Provider Rules

```
✅ Retrieves or persists data from external systems
✅ Returns raw data from the source
❌ MUST NOT contain business logic
❌ MUST NOT perform validation
❌ MUST NOT transform data for presentation
❌ MUST NOT call Validators or Transfers
```

```csharp
// Correct
public class MemberProvider
{
    public Task<MemberDbModel> GetByIdAsync(int id, CancellationToken ct) { ... }
    // returns raw DB model — no filtering, no DTO conversion
}

// Wrong
public class MemberProvider
{
    public Task<MemberDTO> GetByIdAsync(int id)  // should not return DTO
    {
        if (id <= 0) throw new Exception(...);   // validation in Provider — FORBIDDEN
        ...
    }
}
```

---

## Validator Rules

```
✅ Validates input before Provider call
✅ Validates external output when correctness must be checked
❌ MUST NOT access external systems or DB
❌ MUST NOT transform data
❌ MUST NOT call Providers or Transfers
```

```csharp
// Correct
public class MemberValidator
{
    public void ValidateCreateInput(MemberCreateRequest request) { ... }
    public void ValidateUpdateInput(MemberUpdateRequest request) { ... }
    public void ValidateAccountFormat(string account) { ... }
}
```

---

## Transfer Rules

```
✅ Converts between: external format ↔ internal model, internal model ↔ DTO, request ↔ input model
❌ MUST NOT access external systems
❌ MUST NOT perform validation
❌ MUST NOT contain business logic
❌ MUST NOT call Providers or Validators
```

```csharp
// Correct
public class MemberTransfer
{
    public MemberModel FromDb(MemberDbModel source) { ... }
    public MemberDTO ToDTO(MemberModel source) { ... }
    public MemberUpdateInput ToUpdateInput(MemberUpdateRequest request) { ... }
}
```

---

## Grouping Rule — by Domain/Entity, NOT by scenario

**One Transfer and one Validator per domain/entity. Separate scenarios by methods, not classes.**

```
✅ Correct grouping
MemberProvider
MemberValidator   ← all Member validation methods here
MemberTransfer    ← all Member mapping methods here

❌ Wrong grouping
MemberDBTransfer       MemberApiTransfer
MemberInputTransfer    MemberOutputTransfer
MemberCreateValidator  MemberUpdateValidator
MemberDBValidator      MemberInputValidator
```

Do NOT split by: DB vs API, input vs output, create vs update, frontend vs backend usage.

---

## Recommended Flow

```
Controller / Application Layer
        ↓
Validator  (validate input)
        ↓
Provider   (fetch / persist data)
        ↓
Transfer   (map to response model)
        ↓
Response
```

Incorrect flows:
```
Provider → validate internally → transform → return   ❌
Service → directly access DB/API                      ❌
Transfer → query database                             ❌
Validator → call Provider                             ❌
```

