## Data Access Conventions

### MySQL
```csharp
// Correct
var cmd = _mysqlManager.CreateDBCommand(connectId);
cmd.CommandText = "SELECT ...";
cmd.AddParameter("@userId", MySqlDbType.Int32, userId);
await cmd.ExecuteEntityAsync<UserDbModel>();

// Wrong — inline SQL in Service, or using Dapper/EF
```
- All access through `IMySQLManager` + `IMySQLCommand`
- SQL stays in Provider classes under `*.Infrastructure/DataAccess`
- Do NOT inline SQL in Service classes

### Redis
```csharp
// Key format: {Module}:{Feature}:{Key}
var key = $"member:profile:{userId}";
// Always specify expiration when writing
await _redisDb.SetAsync(key, value, TimeSpan.FromMinutes(30));
```

### Cassandra
```csharp
// Always include partition key in queries
// Avoid full table scans
var session = _cassandraManager.CreateSession(keyspace);
session.CommandText = "SELECT ... WHERE partition_key = ?";
```

### PostgreSQL
```csharp
var cmd = _pgManager.CreateDBCommand(connectId);
cmd.CommandText = "SELECT ...";
cmd.AddParameter("userId", userId);
await cmd.ExecuteEntityAsync<UserDbModel>();
```

